# Hartree-Fock on helium with regularized (nemo) orbitals and a protocol ladder
# that CHANGES k between rungs -- deliberately leaving `k` at its -1 default so
# SCF::set_protocol derives it from each threshold (1e-4 -> k=6, 1e-6 -> k=8).
#
# This is the one deck that exercises a varying k in nemo; every other nemo case
# pins `k`, which is why the path was broken and unnoticed for so long. Two
# things had to be fixed to make it work, and both regress silently:
#
#   * the nemos and the AO basis must be reprojected onto the new k when the
#     protocol advances (NemoBase::set_protocol / reproject_mos), and
#   * NuclearCorrelationFactor::initialize must replace its U1 potentials rather
#     than append to them, since U1(axis) reads the first three entries.
#
# The energy must match nemo_he_hf, which reaches the same answer with k pinned
# at 7 -- that agreement is the point of the case. DO NOT add a `k` line here.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc --wf=nemo nemo_he_varyk.in)

dft
    xc        hf
    protocol  [1e-4, 1e-6]
    maxiter   10
    dconv     1e-3
end

nemo
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    eprec   1e-6
    He  0.0  0.0  0.0
end
